{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789214104,"nonce":"focakn1enyk/sAOFnZfAMiO0vbI=","message":"Fixed in c2b5183 by sharing one allocation (allocate_air_registers) between translate_air_v2 and build_air_osr_body: minted constants get their globals first, and a value with lanes \u003e= 2 is allocated as a vector slot from the start rather than re-typed afterwards. The emit_air_vector comment that claimed this was true before was the only thing that was.\n\nNot demonstrated with a widened whole-function lowering: no program in the test corpus is widened on the AOT path (no vector types in any of the 79 unoptimised IR dumps, including test_vectorize), so the corpus IR is byte-identical before and after, and the OSR tests are what exercise the shared code. A fixture that the widener accepts at O3 would be the way to make this observable.","files":null}]}